PART 5: CONTROLLED COMPONENTS
================================================================================

WHAT IS A CONTROLLED COMPONENT?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A controlled component is an input whose value is managed by React state.

Characteristics:

• Value from State
  - Input value comes from a React state variable

• Updated via onChange
  - User input updates state through an event handler

• Single Source of Truth
  - React state determines the input value

• Predictable Behavior
  - Application state contains the current input value

• Easy to Validate
  - Input can be validated during interaction

• Managed by React
  - React state controls the displayed value


CONTROLLED VS UNCONTROLLED COMPONENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+------------------+----------------------------+----------------------------+
| ASPECT           | CONTROLLED                 | UNCONTROLLED               |
+------------------+----------------------------+----------------------------+
| Value Source     | React state                | DOM element                |
| Update           | onChange + state setter    | DOM manages value          |
| React Awareness  | State contains value       | Access when needed         |
| Validation       | Straightforward            | Requires reading DOM/value |
| Initial Value    | value/state                | defaultValue               |
| Common Use       | Most interactive forms     | Simple/special cases       |
| Data Flow        | State drives input value   | DOM maintains input state  |
+------------------+----------------------------+----------------------------+


