PART 8: BEST PRACTICES FOR STATE MANAGEMENT
================================================================================

STATE MANAGEMENT BEST PRACTICES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

+----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+
| PRACTICE             | WHY IT MATTERS           | EXAMPLE                     |
+----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+
| Keep state minimal   | Easier to manage/debug   | Store only changing data    |
| Descriptive names    | Clear code intent        | isLoading                   |
| Initialize properly  | Predictable state        | useState(0)                 |
| Update immutably     | Avoid mutation issues    | {...state, field: value}    |
| Validate data        | Improve data quality     | Check before update         |
| Group related state  | Organized structure      | form object                 |
| Avoid prop drilling  | Cleaner deep sharing     | Context where appropriate   |
| Document state shape | Maintainability          | Comment complex structures  |
| Use custom hooks     | Reusable state logic     | useForm, useAuth            |
| Lift state up        | Share state              | Parent owns shared state    |
+----------------------+--------------------------+-----------------------------+


KEY PRINCIPLES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Minimize State
  - Store only information that needs to change and be remembered

• Use Clear Names
  - Make each state's purpose obvious

• Initialize Correctly
  - Provide appropriate initial values

• Update Immutably
  - Avoid directly mutating arrays and objects in state

• Validate Data
  - Check values where appropriate before accepting/submitting them

• Group Logically
  - Keep related state organized

• Avoid Excessive Prop Drilling
  - Consider Context or other state-sharing patterns when appropriate

• Document Structure
  - Explain complicated state shapes

• Create Custom Hooks
  - Extract reusable stateful logic

• Lift State When Needed
  - Move shared state to a common parent


